 "evidence": {
  "_how": "Three kinds of ground truth, kept apart. [rom] the game's own code, read with a hand-written Thumb decoder (scratch only): SetBoxMonData ROM 0x1ebb70 with jump tables at 0x7c6bb0 (field ids 0-14) and 0x7c6a58 (ids 16-101), SetMonData 0x1ec1bc (table 0x7c6bec), GetBoxMonDataAt 0x20567a, FlagGet 0x132f14. [game] the real game (mGBA wasm core, deterministic) booted on a save the encoder wrote, CONTINUE pressed, Summary pages photographed; the typed values in oracle.* come from those PNGs. [ram] the running game's EWRAM compared byte for byte with the encoder's record. None of this is vanilla pokeemerald unverified.",
  "container": {
   "layoutTable": "[rom] 14 x {u16 offset, u16 size} at ROM 0xF32F6C (the importer reads it from the ROM it is given and checks the contiguous runs of SaveBlock1 ids 1-4 and PokemonStorage ids 5-13); sizes 0xB30, 0xF80 x3 + 0xDD4 = 0x3C54, 0xF80 x9 = 0x8B80.",
   "footerAndChecksum": "[game] a save written by the game itself (tools/pokemonarena_savegen.mjs plays the new game in the core): 14 of 14 sectors of slot 1 verify with footer {id u16 @0xFF4, checksum u16 @0xFF6, signature 0x08012025 @0xFF8, counter u32 @0xFFC} and checksum = fold16(sum of u32 words over the section size).",
   "slotOfRealSave": "[game] the real save sits in slot 1 (counter 1); slot 0 is erased flash."
  },
  "blocks": {
   "party": "[game] SaveBlock1 +0x234 u32 count, +0x238 party records at stride 96 (6-Pokemon party displayed correctly in the Summary screens, batch 'fields').",
   "boxes": "[rom] GetBoxMonDataAt (0x20567a): box b slot p is at gPokemonStoragePtr + 4 + b*0x8E8 + p*76 for b <= 14, p <= 29 (ids 15-18 are RAM-only scratch areas past the saved 0x8B80 bytes); [ram] 10 encoder-placed records, corners and middles of boxes 1-15, found byte for byte at those addresses in the running game; box names 9 bytes each at +0x859c (15 names). NOT photographed in the in-game PC screen.",
   "storageTail": "The bytes after the wallpapers (0x8632..0x8B80) hold a 'BX16' tag at 0x87b4 and are not imported."
  },
  "fields": {
   "nature": "[rom] SetBoxMonData case 12: byte 0x14 bits 3-7 = (personality % 25) XOR nature. [game] pid%25 5 ^ delta 3 -> Docile, 24 ^ 31 -> Relaxed (batch 'misc'); a result of 25+ RESETS the console (observed), so such a record is rejected, never guessed.",
   "shiny": "[rom] case 11: u16@0x1e bit 14 (byte 0x1f bit 6) = natural XOR desired, natural = ((tid ^ sid ^ pid_hi ^ pid_lo) < T), T = 512, or 256 when story flag 0x95e is set (FlagGet reads SaveBlock1[0x1898 + (id>>3)] bit id&7 = byte 0x19c3 bit 6). [game] Pidgey sprite palettes in batches 'shiny-flag-set' (the real save has the flag set) and 'shiny-flag-clear' (same save with the bit cleared): xor 3/255 shiny, 256+ normal with the flag; 255..511 shiny without it; modifier XORs (xor 3 + modifier = normal, xor 600 + modifier = shiny).",
   "ability": "[rom] case 56: record byte 0x33 bits 4-5 (the top nibble of move 4's word). [game] Pidgey 1/2/3 -> Tangled Feet / Big Pecks / Big Pecks; Sprigatito 1 -> Overgrow (empty slot walks down), 2 -> Protean.",
   "hyperTraining": "[rom] cases 91-96: single flag bits 0x33.6 hp, 0x33.7 atk, 0x34.7 def, 0x35.7 spe, 0x36.7 spa, 0x37.7 spd. [game] each flag makes exactly that stat's IV read 31 on the IV page and in the stats (stored IV 0), batches 'hyper' and 'misc'.",
   "moves": "[rom] cases 21-24: four u16 at 0x2c..0x33, each keeps only 11 bits; the 5 spare high bits of each word hold other fields (ability/hyper flags for move 4, location bits for move 3, others). [game] junk in them leaves the four moves unchanged (batch 'misc', moveJunk).",
   "pp": "[rom] cases 25-28: PP bytes 0x34..0x37 keep 7 bits, bit 7 of each is a separate flag (hyper-training for slots 2-4 above).",
   "ppBonuses": "[rom] case 29: byte 0x2a. [game] max PP 15/36/21/24 for 0/1/2/3 ups (batch 'fields' Pikachu); the same byte at the old +0x28 changes nothing.",
   "experience": "[rom] case 33: 24 bits at 0x24 (the top byte is preserved for other data). [game] bit 21 counts (27000 + 2^21 = 2124152 points, Lv100), bit 31 and the top byte do not, 0xFFFFFF is Lv100.",
   "level": "[game] the stored level byte (0x50) is ignored: level comes from EXP and the growth rate.",
   "egg": "[rom] case 55 sets BOTH byte 0x15 bit 2 and IV-word bit 30. [game] IV bit 30 alone draws the Egg page; the flag byte alone draws a normal page named 'Egg'; either rejects the Pokemon (mon.egg).",
   "gender": "[game] personality low byte >= species gender ratio is male (Pidgey, ratio 127: 126 female, 127/128 male).",
   "speciesItemBall": "[rom] cases 18/19/48/100: species 11 bits @0x20, tera 5 bits @0x21 high, held item 10 bits @0x22, ball 6 bits. [game] species ids above 1023 display.",
   "ivEv": "[rom] cases 34-39 EVs at 0x38..0x3d (hp, atk, def, spe, spa, spd); cases 49-54 IVs 5 bits each from 0x48 (hp, atk, def, spe, spa, spd). [game] batches 'fields' and 'hyper'."
  },
  "notDecoded": "Not imported and not decoded: u16 @0x28 (10-bit item-like field), contest stats 0x3e..0x43, pokerus 0x44, met location (0x45 + bit 2 of 0x29 + spare move bits), origins 0x46, hpLost, markings, daysSinceFormChange, IV-word bit 31 and byte 0x1f bit 7 / 0x47 bit 3 (no stat or screen effect seen)."
 },
